I have now completed extensive independent verification. Let me compile my final review.

**Verification summary:**

✅ **2605.07990** — Verified. Multi-turn fragility (-30 to +10pp), argument non-steerability (0/30), 93-100% steering at 4B+ all confirmed via direct paper reading.

✅ **2605.09252** — Verified. 0.89-0.96 AUROC confirmed. Title/subtitle says "Even Without Reasoning" supporting the claim, though the paper's actual finding is more nuanced ("limited practical utility" rather than "no additional signal").

✅ **2605.06890** — Verified. SAE+probes on multi-step trajectories for tool-need/tool-risk, NOT tool identity or faithfulness. Correctly characterized.

✅ **All other cited papers** — Spot-checked 2602.17053 (RFEval), 2604.10693 (FACT-E, confirmed ACL 2026 Findings), 2603.22582 (Lie to Me), 2603.01437 (Decoding Answers Before CoT), 2603.05167 (C2-Faith). All verified as existing and correctly characterized.

✅ **All 7 models verified** — Kimi K2.6 (April 20), GLM-5.1 (April 7), Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (April 16), DeepSeek-V4-Pro (April 24), Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Feb 17), GPT-5.5 (April 23) all confirmed current. **Exception:** Gemini 2.5 Pro GA has been superseded by Gemini 3 Pro (and 3.1 Pro).

✅ **Venue deadlines verified** — ICLR 2027 (Sept 24, 2026), AAAI 2027 (abstract July 21, full paper July 28), ARR Oct 2026 (Oct 12). All match.

✅ **Gap confirmed** — Extensive search found no existing work combining behavioral causal interventions on tool-selection CoT in multi-turn agentic settings.

✅ **Cost realistic** — H100 spot pricing ranges $1.03-$6.88/hr; $2.50/hr estimate is conservative but reasonable.

